From: Waltteri Hooli <1420194+wahooli@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8450: add CPU capacities and power coefficients

sm8450.dtsi gives its CPUs no capacity-dmips-mhz, so every core reports
a cpu_capacity of 1024 and the scheduler treats the four Cortex-A510s
like the Cortex-X2. It has no energy model either, so EAS stays off and
a busy thread lands on whichever core is free.

On the AYANEO Pocket VERT (SM8475) this halved a game's frame rate: the
main thread of Horizon Chase Turbo, running under x86 emulation, spent
about half its time on the A510s. Pinning it to CPUs 4-7 took the game
from ~20 to ~60 fps.

The values are the stock Android device tree's for the same cores:
A510 1024 / 100, A710 2253 / 257, X2 2386 / 509.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8450.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8450.dtsi
@@ -61,6 +61,8 @@
 			power-domains = <&cpu_pd0>;
 			power-domain-names = "psci";
 			qcom,freq-domain = <&cpufreq_hw 0>;
+			capacity-dmips-mhz = <1024>;
+			dynamic-power-coefficient = <100>;
 			#cooling-cells = <2>;
 			clocks = <&cpufreq_hw 0>;
 			l2_0: l2-cache {
@@ -85,6 +87,8 @@
